        "subcategory": "Sacred Lake & Temple",
        "description": "Pushkar Lake is one of Hinduism's most sacred lakes, believed created when Lord Brahma dropped a lotus flower. The town has 52 bathing ghats and the only Brahma Temple in the world. The annual Pushkar Camel Fair draws visitors worldwide.",
        "history": "<p>When <strong>Various rulers over centuries</strong> commissioned the construction of <strong>Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</strong> in <strong>14th Century (Temple), Ancient (Lake)</strong>, the ambition was to create a monument that would reflect the power and cultural sophistication of Pushkar for generations to come. Pushkar Lake is one of Hinduism's most sacred lakes, believed created when Lord Brahma dropped a lotus flower. The town has 52 bathing ghats and the only Brahma Temple in the world. The annual Pushkar Camel Fair draws visitors worldwide. Centuries later, this vision stands magnificently fulfilled — Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple now welcomes hundreds of thousands of visitors annually who come to experience the extraordinary fusion of history, art, and architecture that defines this incomparable landmark.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Structural Wonders of Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</h3><p>The <strong>Temple Architecture</strong> heritage visible throughout <strong>Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</strong> represents one of Rajasthan's finest contributions to world architecture. Commissioned by <strong>Various rulers over centuries</strong> in <strong>14th Century (Temple), Ancient (Lake)</strong>, this temple was designed not merely as a functional space but as an architectural statement — a declaration in stone of the sophistication and cultural refinement of Pushkar's ruling dynasty. The craftsmanship in every corner reflects the extraordinary talent of artisans who were drawn from across Rajputana to contribute their finest skills to this ambitious royal project.</p>\n          \n          <p>Through the centuries, <strong>Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</strong> has witnessed the full arc of Rajasthan's history — periods of great prosperity, times of political upheaval, and the gradual transformation of Pushkar from a medieval royal capital into a modern metropolis. The temple served as the backdrop for countless significant events and royal ceremonies that shaped the destiny of the region. Its walls carry the silent memory of rulers, nobles, and common people whose lives intersected with this remarkable landmark across many generations.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Must-See Features of Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</h3><p>No visit to <strong>Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</strong> is complete without experiencing its most iconic features. The <strong>Only Brahma Temple in World</strong> is widely regarded as the crown jewel of the entire complex, leaving countless visitors speechless with its beauty and craftsmanship. Equally remarkable is the <strong>Sacred Lake with 52 Ghats</strong>, which showcases the extraordinary technical skill and artistic vision that <strong>Various rulers over centuries</strong> inspired in the craftsmen of Pushkar. The unforgettable experience of attending prayers and experiencing the serene atmosphere adds yet another dimension to what is already a deeply enriching visit.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Your Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple Experience Awaits</h3><p>The heritage authorities responsible for <strong>Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple</strong> have worked diligently to ensure visitors receive a world-class experience honouring both the monument's historical importance and the expectations of modern tourism. Pushkar Camel Fair (November) is the most vibrant time. Kartik Purnima (Nov full moon) is holiest. For those wishing to engage most deeply with its history and architecture, guided tours by certified local experts are available and strongly recommended. Plan your visit for <strong>Half Day</strong> and bring a sense of curiosity — Pushkar Lake & Brahma Temple consistently rewards those who look closely and ask questions.</p>",
