        "description": "Jaigarh Fort stands high above Amber Fort and was built as a military stronghold to protect the Amber kingdom. It is famous for housing Jaivana Cannon, once considered the world's largest cannon on wheels.",
        "history": "<p>Rising majestically in <strong>Jaipur</strong>, Rajasthan, <strong>Jaigarh Fort</strong> is a timeless tribute to its founder <strong>Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II</strong>, who ordered its construction in <strong>1726 AD</strong>. Jaigarh Fort stands high above Amber Fort and was built as a military stronghold to protect the Amber kingdom. It is famous for housing Jaivana Cannon, once considered the world's largest cannon on wheels. Recognised today as Main defensive fort of Amber kingdom, this remarkable structure has earned its place among the most celebrated destinations in all of India, drawing scholars, historians, and travellers from every corner of the globe.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Jaigarh Fort — Rajput Military Architecture Architecture at Its Finest</h3><p>What makes <strong>Jaigarh Fort</strong> architecturally extraordinary is the way its <strong>Rajput Military Architecture</strong> design traditions have been applied with such precision and artistry. The builders who worked under the patronage of <strong>Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II</strong> were masters of their craft — every carved surface, every proportioned arch, and every perfectly planned courtyard speaks of decades of accumulated knowledge in stone-working and spatial design. The result continues to astonish architects and historians even by contemporary standards.</p>\n          \n          <p>The role of <strong>Jaigarh Fort</strong> in shaping Jaipur's cultural and political landscape cannot be overstated. From the moment <strong>Maharaja Sawai Jai Singh II</strong> unveiled it in <strong>1726 AD</strong>, this fort became inseparable from the identity of the entire region. It served as the stage for royal coronations, grand durbars, and important religious ceremonies that defined the rhythms of Rajputana life for centuries. Even in times of conflict, Jaigarh Fort stood firm as a symbol of continuity and cultural resilience.</p>\n          \n          <h3>The Finest Features of Jaigarh Fort</h3><p>The range of extraordinary sights at <strong>Jaigarh Fort</strong> ensures that every visitor carries something unique away with them. The magnificent <strong>Jaivana Cannon</strong> has long been the centrepiece of the entire complex — so remarkable that it alone has been the subject of scholarly studies and artistic tributes for decades. The equally impressive <strong>Panoramic Hill Views</strong> showcases a different facet of the <strong>Rajput Military Architecture</strong> tradition that makes Jaigarh Fort such a rich experience. The <strong>Underground Passages to Amber</strong> rounds off a trio of must-see attractions central to any thorough exploration of this iconic Jaipur landmark.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Planning Your Visit to Jaigarh Fort</h3><p>Today, <strong>Jaigarh Fort</strong> welcomes visitors from across India and around the world who come to experience the enduring magic of Jaipur's most cherished heritage. Visit in the morning or late afternoon for the best views and cooler weather. Plan to spend at least <strong>2 Hours</strong> to do justice to everything this remarkable fort has to offer — rushing through would mean missing the countless details that collectively make it one of Rajasthan's greatest treasures.</p>",
