        "history": "<p>Rising majestically in <strong>Udaipur</strong>, Rajasthan, <strong>Saheliyon Ki Bari</strong> is a timeless tribute to its founder <strong>Maharana Sangram Singh</strong>, who ordered its construction in <strong>18th Century</strong>. Saheliyon Ki Bari is a historic garden built for the royal ladies of Udaipur. It is famous for lotus pools, marble pavilions, elephant fountains and manicured lawns. Recognised today as Leisure garden for royal women of Udaipur, this remarkable structure has earned its place among the most celebrated destinations in all of India, drawing scholars, historians, and travellers from every corner of the globe.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Saheliyon Ki Bari — Royal Garden Design Architecture at Its Finest</h3><p>What makes <strong>Saheliyon Ki Bari</strong> architecturally extraordinary is the way its <strong>Royal Garden Design</strong> design traditions have been applied with such precision and artistry. The builders who worked under the patronage of <strong>Maharana Sangram Singh</strong> were masters of their craft — every carved surface, every proportioned arch, and every perfectly planned courtyard speaks of decades of accumulated knowledge in stone-working and spatial design. The result continues to astonish architects and historians even by contemporary standards.</p>\n          \n          <p>The role of <strong>Saheliyon Ki Bari</strong> in shaping Udaipur's cultural and political landscape cannot be overstated. From the moment <strong>Maharana Sangram Singh</strong> unveiled it in <strong>18th Century</strong>, this heritage became inseparable from the identity of the entire region. It served as the stage for royal coronations, grand durbars, and important religious ceremonies that defined the rhythms of Rajputana life for centuries. Even in times of conflict, Saheliyon Ki Bari stood firm as a symbol of continuity and cultural resilience.</p>\n          \n          <h3>The Finest Features of Saheliyon Ki Bari</h3><p>The range of extraordinary sights at <strong>Saheliyon Ki Bari</strong> ensures that every visitor carries something unique away with them. The magnificent <strong>Lotus Pools</strong> has long been the centrepiece of the entire complex — so remarkable that it alone has been the subject of scholarly studies and artistic tributes for decades. The equally impressive <strong>Marble Pavilions</strong> showcases a different facet of the <strong>Royal Garden Design</strong> tradition that makes Saheliyon Ki Bari such a rich experience. The <strong>Elephant Fountains</strong> rounds off a trio of must-see attractions central to any thorough exploration of this iconic Udaipur landmark.</p>\n          \n          <h3>Planning Your Visit to Saheliyon Ki Bari</h3><p>Today, <strong>Saheliyon Ki Bari</strong> welcomes visitors from across India and around the world who come to experience the enduring magic of Udaipur's most cherished heritage. Visit early morning for quiet gardens and fresh light. Plan to spend at least <strong>1 Hour</strong> to do justice to everything this remarkable heritage has to offer — rushing through would mean missing the countless details that collectively make it one of Rajasthan's greatest treasures.</p>",
